    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Josefa Teotalco was an unpious nun Embraced for a forgotten scheme requiring an all-nun auxiliary; despite being a comparatively weak 14th-generation Cainite, she found genuine power through Noddist devotion, joining Las Hermanitas de Zila. During the Ravnos antitribu's 1999 Week of Nightmares frenzy she experienced visions of Gehenna, emerged transformed, and diablerized her own pack priest in Monomacy when the woman doubted her.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>Josefa now preaches with rising charismatic fervor that the Sabbat must abandon strategy and Path philosophy alike and fight the Antediluvians with everything, now, because there is no tomorrow. An unnamed elder (one of the city's three senior prisci, at the Storyteller's choice) secretly feeds her distorted Noddist lore and rhetoric to use her as an unwitting mouthpiece, exploiting the fact that lowering her generation cost Josefa the intuitive sense for others' hidden agendas she once had.</p>",
    "notes": "Sire: Luisa Montoya. Merit: Face the Flames (two extra dice resisting Rötschreck from fire, atop her already-high Courage and Fire Dancing).",
